# L9 Repository Chassis — l9-repo-template

> This file is generated from .cursor/rules/templates/*.mdc.template. Do not edit directly; edit the template or plugin-config.yaml.

## Identity

- This repository carries the generic L9 repository chassis assembled by the L9 repository birth factory.
- What semantic product it is (ProductKind, archetype, Gate or SDK obligations) is declared
  by the product's resolved semantics upstream (`Quantum-L9/.github` `semantics/`). This rule
  does not infer it from repository shape, package contents, SDK presence, or Gate presence.

## Forbidden (chassis)

- Repository-local CI orchestration — CI execution semantics belong to l9-ci-core
- A second task runner beside `make` (Justfile)
- Re-vendoring a repository-execution runtime under `tools/` (V2 runtime is Core-owned)
- Hand-editing generated `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`

## Required habits

- Package: `l9_example_pkg`
- No `eval()` / `exec()` / `print()` in `src/`
- Prefer `settings.validate_safe()`, structured errors, immutable health snapshots
- Run `make verify` (or `make pr-check`) before claiming done
- Hand-edit templates under `.cursor/rules/templates/`, not generated `.mdc`
